ence": "medium", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Incumbent Glenn Grothman (R) is running."]}, "overview": "Glenn Grothman, the Republican incumbent, is favored to win re-election in this R+8 eastern Wisconsin district. Nine raters unanimously place the race on the Republican side, most calling it Safe or Solid Republican, and prediction markets give Democrats only about a 6 percent chance. Grothman has raised roughly $929,000 and holds $830,000 on hand, dwarfing Democrat Brad Smith's $166,000 raised. The only usable public poll, a Democratic-sponsored survey from May, showed Grothman leading 61 to 39.\n\nSmith won a contested August primary and has earned the Wisconsin AFL-CIO endorsement, but enters the general election with limited resources and little name recognition. Independent Michael Thurow has raised nearly $170,000 and could siphon some votes, though he is unlikely to change the outcome. A Democratic-leaning national environment offers the party its clearest path to keeping the final margin closer than the district's fundamentals suggest.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.0556, "margin": -10.42}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.0454, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.0701, "margin": -11.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.063, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.0353, "margin": -12.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.0532, "margin": -11.5}]}